---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { url } from "../lib/site";
---

<Layout
	title="Terms of Service - NoteGuard"
	description="The terms that apply when you download and use NoteGuard, the private, offline notes app for Android."
>
	<main>
		<PageHeader
			eyebrow="Legal"
			title="Terms of Service"
			lede="These terms cover the NoteGuard app and this website. They are short because there is not much to say about an app that has no account and sends nothing anywhere."
			meta="Last updated: November 10, 2026."
		/>

		<div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-3xl pb-24">
			<div class="legal">
				<section class="mb-10">
					<h2>1. Agreement to these terms</h2>
					<p>
						By downloading or using NoteGuard, you agree to these terms.
						Please read them before you use the app. If you do not agree
						with them, do not use the app — and if you already do, you
						can simply uninstall it and delete your vault folder.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section class="mb-10">
					<h2>2. The service</h2>
					<p>
						NoteGuard is a note-taking application for Android, provided
						free of charge. It is not a hosted service: there is no
						account, no subscription tier, and no server that holds
						your notes. The app is provided as-is, with the features
						described on this site and in the release notes.
					</p>
					<p>
						You may use the app for any lawful purpose. You may not
						redistribute it, use it to break the law, or attempt to
						remove or alter the protections described in the security
						section of this site.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section class="mb-10">
					<h2>3. Your content</h2>
					<p>
						You retain all rights and ownership of the notes, audio,
						images and other content you create in NoteGuard. We claim
						no licence over it and receive no copy of it.
					</p>
					<p>
						Because NoteGuard is a local-only app, you are responsible
						for backing up your data. We are not responsible for data
						loss caused by device failure, uninstalling the app,
						deleting the vault folder, or a lost backup. Back up by
						copying your vault folder, and keep a copy somewhere you
						trust.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section class="mb-10">
					<h2>4. Locked notes and your PIN</h2>
					<p>
						When you lock a note, the note is encrypted with a key
						derived from the PIN you type, and <strong
							>the PIN is not stored anywhere</strong
						>. There is no stored copy to compare against, no recovery
						code and no reset.
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong
							>You are solely responsible for remembering the PIN
							for a locked note.</strong
						>
						A forgotten PIN means the note cannot be read — not by you,
						not by us, and not by anyone else. We cannot recover it,
						because we never had it. The same applies to a locked note
						whose PIN is known only to you and has been lost.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section class="mb-10">
					<h2>5. On-device AI and downloaded models</h2>
					<p>
						NoteGuard's AI features run entirely on your device using
						model files that you download from inside the app. Model
						files are fetched from the model publishers' distribution
						hosting, which is the only third-party download the app
						performs, along with a web page you choose to paste and
						ask it to summarise.
					</p>
					<p>
						AI output is produced by probabilistic models. It can be
						inaccurate, out of date, or plainly wrong. Verify anything
						important before you rely on it, and do not use it as the
						sole basis for a decision. Image generation in particular
						is slow and experimental.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section class="mb-10">
					<h2>6. Third-party content</h2>
					<p>
						Notes you import, links you paste and pages you fetch are
						subject to the rights and terms of whoever published
						them. You are responsible for how you use that content,
						and for any export or share you make of it.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section class="mb-10">
					<h2>7. No warranty</h2>
					<p>
						The app is provided "as is" and "as available", without
						warranty of any kind, express or implied. We do not
						warrant that it will be uninterrupted, error-free, or
						that it will never lose data. Encryption and security
						features are described honestly, including their limits,
						but no system can promise absolute security.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section class="mb-10">
					<h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
					<p>
						To the fullest extent permitted by law, we are not liable
						for any indirect, incidental, special or consequential
						loss arising from your use of NoteGuard, including lost
						notes, lost data, lost profits, or a lost PIN. Nothing in
						these terms limits liability that cannot lawfully be
						limited.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section class="mb-10">
					<h2>9. Changes</h2>
					<p>
						We may update these terms, and we may update the app, at
						any time. The current terms are always published on this
						page with the date they were last updated. Your continued
						use of the app after a change means you accept the
						updated terms.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section class="mb-10">
					<h2>10. Contact</h2>
					<p>
						Questions about these terms can be raised as an issue on
						the project's GitHub page at
						<a href="https://github.com/heymeowcat" rel="noopener"
							>github.com/heymeowcat</a
						>.
					</p>
				</section>
			</div>

			<a
				href={url("/")}
				class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-purple-300 hover:text-purple-200 transition-colors"
			>
				← Back to NoteGuard
			</a>
		</div>
	</main>
	<Footer />
</Layout>
